From 4e4b88aa73f4291c5089dc4cb440f76d2bfcd100 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 08:44:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add per-widget show/hide toggles for the Dashboard, in
 Settings > Dashboard

Fills in the previously-placeholder Dashboard settings tab with a switch
for each of the five Dashboard widgets: Quick Glance Row, Recently Added,
Site Blocks by Type, Certificate Status, and Upstream Health. All default
to shown, so an existing config.json with no dashboard_widgets entry (or
one missing a key for a widget added later) behaves exactly as before.

Also fixes dashboard-stats.js's live-refresh guard, which previously
bailed out entirely whenever the Current Requests span was missing --
that's now possible on its own whenever Quick Glance Row is turned off,
which would have silently stopped the Upstream Health card from
refreshing too even when that widget is still on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GdhKf193j6ggwAGFYCUaJg
